<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Partial Info.plist for keys that have no INFOPLIST_KEY_* build-setting
  equivalent (or belong together with one that doesn't). The rest of the
  Info.plist is still generated (GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE: YES in
  project.yml); Xcode merges this file's keys on top of the generated ones.
  Do NOT add CFBundle* version/identity keys here — they would override the
  MARKETING_VERSION / CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION build settings.

  All three keys serve "Sync from computer" (QR snapshot sync):
  - NSCameraUsageDescription: scanning the QR code.
  - NSAppTransportSecurity/NSAllowsLocalNetworking: the QR encodes a plain
    http:// URL to a one-shot server on the user's Mac (LAN only) —
    scoped local-networking ATS exception, NOT NSAllowsArbitraryLoads.
  - NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription: iOS's local-network privacy prompt
    fires on direct connections to LAN addresses.
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Scan the QR code shown by DVM Finance on your computer to sync data.</string>
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DVM Finance downloads the snapshot directly from DVM Finance on your computer over your local network.</string>
	<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
